      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_1",
          "text": "The chapter\u2019s meal conflict is not only about correct words or ritual form. Paul describes some people eating their own supper while others remain hungry or are humiliated, then places the received tradition about bread, cup, remembrance, and the new covenant inside that rebuke. The Lord\u2019s supper cannot be separated from material regard for the people who gather.",
