      "kind": "historical_context",
      "title": "The chapter\u2019s wider scriptural frame",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_3",
          "text": "First Corinthians embeds related meal traditions within a conflict over unequal access, hunger, humiliation, and communal discernment. Its image-of-God language also belongs to a larger scriptural movement in which humanity receives a representative vocation that is later described as marred and renewed. Baptismal and communal language provides a wider setting for identity, but it should not replace the chapter\u2019s direct concern with the assembly\u2019s shared meal.",
