      "title": "Head presentation and mutuality",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_4",
          "text": "The head-presentation discussion assumes that women pray and prophesy while it considers covering, hair, shame, glory, nature, and custom. The force of kephale remains disputed, and the argument also states that woman and man are not independent in the Lord, pairing creation origin with birth from woman. Any hierarchy reading must account for this reciprocal dependence and for women\u2019s Spirit-related speech rather than turning the passage into a total speech ban.",
