          "id": "block_6",
          "text": "The same verb can order silence for an uninterpreted tongue speaker, a prophet when another receives revelation, and women or wives in a passage whose activity and scope remain disputed. Chapter 11\u2019s assumption that women pray and prophesy means later silence language requires qualified interpretation rather than a simple conversion of women into a permanently voiceless class.",
